Send a real postcode on whitelabelled DPD collection addresses (v0.111)

The v0.109 Whitelabel toggle sent "-" for street/town, GB for country, and
left postcode out entirely along with organisation/locality/county. The
user manually tested against the real DPD API by blanking every sender
field except street="-", town="-", postcode="PR2 5BL" (the Preston depot)
and country="GB", and confirmed that's what actually gets a properly
sorted/routed label - DPD still needs a genuine postcode to route the
parcel even with the rest of the visible address dashed out or blank.

Added a new dpd_whitelabel_postcode setting, sent as the collection
address's postcode whenever Whitelabel is on (organisation/locality/county
are still left out entirely). Defaults to PR2 5BL but is editable in
Settings > DPD, in a new field that only appears while the Whitelabel
toggle is checked.

